<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa in code-sharing with Thai Airways.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa in code-sharing with Thai Airways.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German airline Deutsche Lufthansa AG said it had signed a code-sharing agreement with partner Thai Airways to cover destinations in Bangladesh, Brunei, Laos and Nepal.</p>
<p>It said the arrangement, starting April 28, would allow Lufthansa passengers to fly from Munich via Bangkok to Bandar Seri Begawan in Brunei, Dhaka in Bangladesh, Vientiane in Laos and Katmandu in Nepal.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
